        "math_academy_id": "q-255829",
        "problem": "Given that the function $f(x)={e}^{x}-4{x}^{2}$ has a root in the interval $[0,1],$ use the Netwon-Raphson process starting from ${x}_{0}=1$ to estimate the root. Round your final answer to one decimal place.\n\n$x\u2248$\n{{field-1}}",
        "worked_solution": "The formula for the Newton-Raphson method is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-\\frac{f({x}_{n})}{{f}^{\u2032}({x}_{n})}\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}^{\u2032}({x}_{n})$ is the derivative of $f(x)$ evaluated at ${x}_{n}.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{\u2032}(x)=({e}^{x}-4{x}^{2})^{\u2032}={e}^{x}-8x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson formula is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{n+1} & ={x}_{n}-\\frac{{e}^{{x}_{n}}-4{x}_{n}^{2}}{{e}^{{x}_{n}}-8{x}_{n}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}_{n}({e}^{{x}_{n}}-8{x}_{n})-({e}^{{x}_{n}}-4{x}_{n}^{2})}{{e}^{{x}_{n}}-8{x}_{n}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}_{n}{e}^{{x}_{n}}-{e}^{{x}_{n}}-4{x}_{n}^{2}}{{e}^{{x}_{n}}-8{x}_{n}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nStarting with ${x}_{0}=1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =\\frac{{x}_{0}{e}^{{x}_{0}}-{e}^{{x}_{0}}-4{x}_{0}^{2}}{{e}^{{x}_{0}}-8{x}_{0}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1{e}^{1}-{e}^{1}-4(1)^{2}}{{e}^{1}-8(1)} \\\\  & =0.757\u2026.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =\\frac{{x}_{1}{e}^{{x}_{1}}-{e}^{{x}_{1}}-4{x}_{1}^{2}}{{e}^{{x}_{1}}-8{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(0.757\u2026){e}^{0.757\u2026}-{e}^{0.757\u2026}-4(0.757\u2026)^{2}}{{e}^{0.757\u2026}-8(0.757\u2026)} \\\\  & =0.716\u2026, \\\\ {x}_{3} & =\\frac{{x}_{2}{e}^{{x}_{2}}-{e}^{{x}_{2}}-4{x}_{2}^{2}}{{e}^{{x}_{2}}-8{x}_{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(0.716\u2026){e}^{0.716\u2026}-{e}^{0.716\u2026}-4(0.716\u2026)^{2}}{{e}^{0.716\u2026}-8(0.716\u2026)} \\\\  & =0.714\u2026.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the last two approximations ${x}_{2}\u22480.7$ and ${x}_{3}\u22480.7$ are the same when rounded to one decimal place.\n\nTherefore, the root of the function is $x\u22480.7,$ rounded to one decimal place.",
